<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Transforming a school logo</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The art club at a school in Nyeri draws its logo on a grid. One corner of the logo is \(L({@Lp[1]@},\,{@Lp[2]@})\), and the logo's area is \({@ar@}\) square units. To make a banner, the logo is first [[if test="is(t1n=1)"]]stretched with stretch factor \({@k@}\) and the x-axis invariant[[/if]][[if test="is(t1n=2)"]]stretched with stretch factor \({@k@}\) and the y-axis invariant[[/if]][[if test="is(t1n=3)"]]sheared with the x-axis invariant and shear factor \({@k@}\)[[/if]][[if test="is(t1n=4)"]]sheared with the y-axis invariant and shear factor \({@k@}\)[[/if]]. The result then undergoes the [[if test="is(t2=\"rx\")"]]reflection in the x-axis[[/if]][[if test="is(t2=\"ry\")"]]reflection in the y-axis[[/if]][[if test="is(t2=\"ryx\")"]]reflection in the line \(y = x\)[[/if]][[if test="is(t2=\"rmyx\")"]]reflection in the line \(y = -x\)[[/if]][[if test="is(t2=\"r90\")"]]rotation of \(90^\circ\) anticlockwise about O[[/if]][[if test="is(t2=\"r180\")"]]rotation of \(180^\circ\) about O[[/if]][[if test="is(t2=\"r270\")"]]rotation of \(90^\circ\) clockwise about O[[/if]].</p><p>(a) Find the single matrix for the two transformations.</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the image of L on the banner.</p><div>( [[input:ans2]] , [[input:ans3]] ) [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the area of the logo on the banner.</p><div>[[input:ans4]] square units [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) The first matrix is \(A = {@A@}\) and the second is \(B = {@B@}\). The matrix of the transformation done first is written on the right: \(BA = {@B@}{@A@} = {@ta@}\).</p><p>(b) \({@ta@}{@Lc@} = {@ta.Lc@}\), so L goes to \(({@tL[1]@},\,{@tL[2]@})\).</p><p>(c) \(\det(BA) = {@determinant(ta)@}\), so the area scale factor is \({@abs(determinant(ta))@}\) and the area on the banner is \({@abs(determinant(ta))@} \times {@ar@} = {@tar@}\) square units. [[if test="isst"]]The stretch multiplies areas by \({@k@}\); the second transformation does not change area.[[else]]Neither a shear nor a reflection or rotation changes area.[[/if]]</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
near(L,T) := is(abs(L[1]-T[1]) + abs(L[2]-T[2]) < 0.001);
Srx: matrix([1,0],[0,-1]); Sry: matrix([-1,0],[0,1]); Sryx: matrix([0,1],[1,0]); Srmyx: matrix([0,-1],[-1,0]);
Sr90: matrix([0,-1],[1,0]); Sr180: matrix([-1,0],[0,-1]); Sr270: matrix([0,1],[-1,0]);
symkeys: ["rx","ry","ryx","rmyx","r90","r180","r270"];
symmats: [Srx,Sry,Sryx,Srmyx,Sr90,Sr180,Sr270];
sm(k) := symmats[sublist_indices(symkeys, lambda([u], u=k))[1]];
sn(k) := sublist_indices(symkeys, lambda([u], u=k))[1];
skey(A) := block([j], j: sublist_indices(symmats, lambda([u], is(u=A))), if j=[] then "none" else symkeys[j[1]]);
/* Design: a stretch or shear followed by a reflection or rotation. Source: original. First transformation: sx stretch (x-axis invariant), sy stretch (y-axis invariant), hx shear (x-axis invariant), hy shear (y-axis invariant); then a reflection or rotation. A x B, its image, the image after the first only, and the follow-through value are distinct on every entry. PRT3 node 3: for stretch entries the area left unchanged; for shear entries (1 + |k|) times the area (the area is unchanged for a shear, so there is no "forgot" error to name). */
llist: [["sx",2,"r90",[4,1],12],["sy",3/2,"r90",[2,3],15],["hx",1/2,"rx",[1,3],12],["hy",3/2,"ry",[1,3],15],["sx",5/2,"r90",[3,2],12],["hx",-3/2,"r90",[3,2],15],["sy",4,"ryx",[4,2],10],["hy",1/2,"r90",[3,4],15],["sx",1/2,"rmyx",[4,2],15],["hx",5/2,"rmyx",[1,2],10]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
t1: llist[ix][1]; k: llist[ix][2]; t2: llist[ix][3]; Lp: llist[ix][4]; ar: llist[ix][5];
A: if t1="sx" then matrix([1,0],[0,k]) else if t1="sy" then matrix([k,0],[0,1]) else if t1="hx" then matrix([1,k],[0,1]) else matrix([1,0],[k,1]);
B: sm(t2);
Lc: transpose(matrix(Lp));
ta: B.A; tL: list_matrix_entries(ta.Lc);
tar: abs(determinant(ta))*ar;
isst: is(t1="sx" or t1="sy");
/* diagnostics */
AB: A.B; ABL: list_matrix_entries(AB.Lc); AL: list_matrix_entries(A.Lc);
n3v: if isst then ar else (1+abs(k))*ar;
mtar: -tar;
tw: ta+matrix([1,0],[0,0]); twL: list_matrix_entries(tw.Lc); tLw: tL+[0,1]; tarw: tar+1;
t1n: if t1="sx" then 1 else if t1="sy" then 2 else if t1="hx" then 3 else 4;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
